# Byte-pin every file a source scanner reads.
#
# `.cjs` is here because tests/support/app-surface.ts declares it scannable,
# and `.sql` because the lifecycle/deletion registry scanners read the
# migrations (54 of 62 are CRLF in the worktree today). Both were missing
# while this file claimed to cover "every file a source scanner reads".
#
# This project's scanners match multi-line source literals — the catch scan in
# tests/action-gate.test.ts, the null-mapping pin in tests/shell-rail.test.tsx,
# the route and label pins in tests/page-wiring.test.tsx, the bootstrap pin in
# tests/theme.test.ts. `core.autocrlf` is true on this machine, so without an
# attribute those files' worktree bytes are not the bytes git stores, and any
# operation that re-materialises them — a stash apply, a checkout, a branch
# switch, a merge, even an editor save — can flip the line endings underneath a
# scanner. A positive match then goes red on a phantom change, and a negative
# match goes silently GREEN on a real violation.
#
# CLAUDE.md records this twice (2026-09-04, recurred 2026-09-18) and names the
# only two acceptable remedies: pin the bytes here, or normalise \r\n inside
# every scanner. A note to re-check is explicitly not one of them. The repo root
# already pins *.sh, *.md and *.json; the phase-1 reviewer gate found that the
# TypeScript, CSS and SVG this workspace scans were never covered.
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.mts   text eol=lf
*.cts   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.jsx   text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
